hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7096","7135 Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, he said: “Makhzumiya was borrowing some belongings and she denied it, so she was brought to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about her and said: If she were Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, I would cut off her hand. Sufyan was told: Who He mentioned it? He said: Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, God Almighty willing. Muhammad bin Mansour differed from him in his wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7097","7136 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “ That a woman had stolen, so she was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they said: Who dares against the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, unless he Is it Osama? So they spoke to Osama, and he spoke to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Osama, your children have perished. Israel when they were: If a noble person committed a punishment among them, they would abandon him and do not enforce him, and if a lowly person happened to them, they would abide by him, even if it were Fatima. The daughter of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have cut her off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7098","7137 Rizkallah bin Musa informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “A thief was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he cut him off. They said: We did not want you to do this to him. He said: If it had been Fatima, \I would have cut her off\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7099","7138 Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq informed us, saying: Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “A woman stole during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: Who will speak to him about it?” There was no one among us who spoke to him about it, except his love, Osama. So he spoke to him and said: O Osama, the children of Israel were destroyed by something like this. It was If the noble among them steals, they leave him, and if the weak, lowly among them steals, they cut him off. And if she had been Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, I would have cut her off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7100","7139 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: “A woman borrowed some jewelry from someone she knew, but she did not know, so she sold it and took its price, and it was brought to the Prophet.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Its people sought Usama bin Zayd, and he spoke to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about him, and the face of the Messenger of God’s face changed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was speaking to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Will you intercede for me regarding one of the limits set by God? Osama said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose on the evening of that day and praised God Almighty as he deserved it. Then he said: As for what follows, the people perished before you, because if the honorable among them stole, they would abandon him, and if the weak among them stole, they would stand against him. The punishment, by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, if Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, had stolen, I would have cut off her hand, then he cut off that woman,” Al-Layth continued. According to his saying: it was stolen (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7101","7140 Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The Quraysh were concerned about the affairs of The Makhzoumiya that was stolen. They said: Who will speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it? They said: And who would dare against him, except Usama bin Zaid? The love of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? So Osama spoke to him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Will you intercede for one of God’s punishments? Then he stood up So he delivered a speech and said: Those before you were destroyed because if the honorable among them stole, they would abandon him, and if the weak among them stole, they would impose punishment on him. By God, if Fatima bint Muhammad had stolen, I would have cut off her hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7102","7141 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu al-Jawab told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “A woman from the Quraysh stole from Banu Makhzum. It was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: Who will speak to him about it? They said: Usama bin Zayd, so he came to him and spoke to him, so he greeted him and said: If the noble among them stole, they would leave him to the children of Israel, and if the lowly among them stole, they would cut him off. By the One in whose hand is my soul, even if Fatima was the daughter of Muhammad. \She stole"
"7103","7142 Muhammad bin Jabla told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa bin Ayan told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Quraysh were concerned about the Makhzumiya that had been stolen, so they said: Who will speak about it? Meaning the Messenger May God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Who would dare him, except Usama bin Zaid, the love of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Usama spoke to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Those before you were destroyed because when a noble person among them stole, they would abandon him, and if he stole among them, they would leave him alone. They imposed the punishment on the weak, and by God, if Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, had stolen, I would have cut off her hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7104","7143 Al-Harith bin Miskin I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Urwah bin Al-Zubayr told him, on the authority of Aisha, “A woman stole during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Battle of Conquest, so she was brought The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Usama bin Zaid spoke to him about it. When he spoke to him, the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, colored, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do you intercede for one of God’s punishments? Osama said to him: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of God. When evening came, he rose. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praised God Almighty for what he deserved, then he said: As for what follows, he only destroyed the people. Before you, if the noble among them stole, they would abandon him, and if the weak among them stole, they would impose the punishment on him. Then he said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, “If Fatima bint Muhammad had stolen, I would have cut off her hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7105","7144 Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa informed me, “that A woman stole from a messenger during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Battle of Conquest, and her people were terrified to go to Usama bin Zayd. They seek intercession through him. Urwa said: When Osama spoke to him about it, the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed, and he said: You are speaking to me about one of the God’s limits? Osama said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of God. When evening came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose to give a sermon and praised God. As he deserved it, then he said: As for what follows, the people before you perished only because when a noble person among them stole, they abandoned him, and when The weak among them stole, they imposed the punishment on him, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, had stolen, I would have cut off her sins. Her hand, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that that woman’s hand be cut off, and her repentance improved after that. Aisha said May God be pleased with her: She would come after that and I would present her needs to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7106","7145 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Issa bin Yazid, he said: Jarir bin Yazid told me that he heard Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir narrates that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A punishment to be applied in “The earth is better for the people of the earth than to have it rain for thirty mornings.” Yunus bin Ubaid stopped him and differed from him in some of his words."
"7107","7146 Amr bin Zurarah informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Plantation, he said: Abu Hurairah said: “Establishing a punishment done to a land is better for its people than rain for forty nights,” and this is correct, and by God. Success"
"7108","7147 Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Hanzalah told us, he said: I heard Nafi’, he said: I heard Abdul Allah ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut a shield whose value was five dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7109","7148 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Hanzalah told us, that Nafi’ told them, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut a shield whose price is three dirhams.”"
"7110","7149 Qutaibah informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cut into a shield whose price was \three dirhams\"""""
"7111","7150 Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail bin Umayyah told me that Nafi’, He told him that Abdullah bin Omar told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “cut off the hand of a thief who stole a shield belonging to women, the price of which was three dirhams (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7112","7151 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, and Ismail bin Umayyah. And Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, 9 and Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was drawn in a shield of the size of \three dirhams\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7113","7152 Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Ali Al-Hanafi told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cut in a spear.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and Shu’bah disagreed with it."
"7114","7153 Ahmad bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Anas, he said: “Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, was cut into pieces in a shield whose value was five dirhams.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is better. Correctly"
"7115","7154 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas say: “A man stole He was free of charge at the time of Abu Bakr, so he paid five dirhams, so he cut him off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7116","7155 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Hassan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut a quarter of a dinar.”"
"7117","7156 Harun bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalid bin Nazar told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Mabrur told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand should not be cut off, except for the price of a shield. A third of a dinar, or half a dinar or more.”"
"7118","7157 Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Amra said: On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The thief’s hand shall be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7119","7158 Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, and Amra, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand of a thief will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.”"
"7120","7159 Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab, who is Ibn Ata’ Al-Khafaf, was weak, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The thief’s hand shall be cut off at a quarter of a dinar or more.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7121","7160 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand of a thief shall be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.”"
"7122","7161 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said “The thief will be punished with a quarter of a dinar or more.”"
"7123","7162 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, and Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give a quarter of a dinar or more.”"
"7124","7163 Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something like this: “The hand of a thief will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7125","7164 Yazid bin Muhammad bin Fudayl told me, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Yahya told us Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand of a thief will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more,” Abu said. Abdul Rahman: Endowed by Ibn Uyaynah and Ibn Al-Mubarak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7126","7165 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, that she heard Aisha, It says: “It is cut at a quarter of a dinar and above.”"
"7127","7166 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, saying: Ibn Dris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The amount is from a quarter of a dinar or more.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7128","7167 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Abd Rabbuh, and Ruzaiq the companion of a deer, They heard about Umrah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The amount is a quarter of a dinar and onwards.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And in Malik’s narration, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, there is evidence that the hadith is raised, and God knows best."
"7129","7168 Al-Harith bin Miskin. A reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “It has not been a long time since I have forgotten, and the pieces are at a quarter of a dinar and onwards.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is the correct view, and a hadith. Aban, and Saeed made a mistake"
"7130","7169 Abu Salih al-Makki Muhammad ibn Zanbur informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The hand of a thief shall not be cut off, except in A quarter of a dinar and onwards.” Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Salman informed me. On the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he read it to us. I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it. He told us: He wants something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7131","7170 Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, On the authority of Amra, she said: Aisha said: “The amount is a quarter of a dinar or more.”"
"7132","7171 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us. Ibn Abi Al-Rijal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand of the thief shall be cut off for the price of The price of the shield is a quarter of a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7133","7172 Yahya bin Durst told me, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Muhammad bin Abd The Most Gracious narrated to him, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to cut off the hand for a quarter of a dinar or more.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7134","7173 Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he mentioned a word meaning on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand should not be cut off.” \Except for a quarter of a dinar.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7135","7174 Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ismail al-Tabarani told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Bahr Abu Ali told us, he said: Mubarak told us Ibn Saad, he said: Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir told me, he said: Ikrimah told me that his wife told him that Aisha’s mother The believers. I told her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hand will be cut off in the shield.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know. Abd al-Rahman bin Bahr, is this man not blessed? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7136","7175 Ubayd Allah bin Saad narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj narrated to him, that Sulaiman bin Yasar narrated to him, that Amra bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that she heard Aisha says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The thief’s hand shall not be cut off below the shield.” Aisha was asked: What is the price of the shield? “A quarter of a dinar.”"
"7137","7176 Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Makhramah informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Yassar, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The hand of a thief shall not be cut off, except for a quarter of a dinar.” And onwards"
"7138","7177 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Qudamah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Makhramah informed us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Othman bin Abi Al-Walid, the client of the Al-Akhnasids, says: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubair, saying: Aisha was speaking, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, it says: “The hand shall not be cut off, except in the case of a jinn, or for its price.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7139","7178 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Qudamah bin Muhammad told me, he said: Makhramah bin Bukair told me, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard Uthman bin Abi Al-Walid saying: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubayr saying: Aisha was speaking, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The hand is not cut off, except for a shield, or its price.” He claimed that Urwa, and he said: A shield is worth four rak’ahs. He said: And I heard Suleiman bin Yasar, claiming that he heard Amra, saying: I heard Aisha, narrating that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “The hand shall not be amputated, except for a quarter of a dinar or more.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7140","7180 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Danaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar said: “Do not cut off the fifth, except in five.” Hammam said: I met Abdullah Al-Danaj and he told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, He said: “Do not cut off the fifth, except in five.”"
"7141","7181 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “No \The hand of a thief shall be cut off in the place of a shield or a shield"
"7142","7182 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Azzah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdul God: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “cut off five dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7143","7183 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ayman, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not cut off a thief except for the price of a shield. He said: The price of a shield on that day was a dinar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7144","7188 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata’, and Mujahid, on the authority of Ayman ibn Umm Ayman, he narrated it. He said: “No pieces, except for the price of a shield, and its price on that day will be a dinar.” Jarir stopped him."
"7145","7190 Ubayd Allah bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told us, Ata bin Abi Rabah told him that Abdullah bin Abbas used to say: “Its price at that time was ten dirhams.” Ibn Numayr disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Ata’"
"7146","7191 Yahya bin Musa told us, he said: Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, similarly: “The price of a shield during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was ten dirhams,” Muhammad told me. Ibn Wahb, he said: Muhammad Ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to me, on the authority of Ayyub Ibn Musa, on the authority of Ata’, mursal, narrated by Abd Al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, who said: (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7147","7193 Siwar bin Abdullah told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, and Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Muhammad Ibn Salam, he said: Ishaq informed us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us about him, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ayman, the client of Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said Khaled, in his hadith: Mawla al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tabi’, on the authority of Ka’b, said: “Whoever performs ablution, performs ablution well and prays,” and Siwar said: Then he prays The last evening prayer, then he prayed four rak’ahs after that, and he completed it. Siwar said: He completes their bowing and prostration, and he knows what he recites. And Siwar said: He says, “In them, it will be for him like the Night of Destiny.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7148","7194 Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ayman, the client of Ibn Omar. On the authority of Tabai’, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “Whoever performs ablution, performs his ablution well, then attends the Umma prayer in congregation, then prays four times like it.” He recites during it, and completes his bowing and prostration, for him will be rewarded like the Night of Decree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7149","7195 Khallad bin Aslam informed us, on the authority of Abdullah, who is Ibn Idris, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: “The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was ten dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7150","7196 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: How often should a hand be cut off? He said: “The hand is not cut off in hanging fruit, if the two branches are attached to it. It is not cut off in the middle of a fruit, and it is not cut off in the case of a mountain, if it shelters it.” The windmills were cut into pieces at the price of a shield.”"
"7151","7197 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was asked about the hanging fruit, and he said: “Whoever gets it from someone in need He did not commit fraud, then there is no blame on him, and whoever takes away any of it must pay a fine and a double penalty, and whoever steals any of it after A slave is sheltering him, and it reaches the price of a shield, so he must cut it off, and whoever steals less than that, he must pay a fine and punishment double it.”"
"7152","7198 Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith and Hisham bin Saad informed me. On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, “A man from Muzainah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, how do you see the Harisah of the Mountain? He said: It and something like it, and the punishment, and there is no cutting on any of the livestock, except for what He sheltered him, and he reached the price of the shield, so in it is the amputation of the hand, and if it does not reach the price of the shield, in it there is a fine of twice as much, and lashes of execution. He said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the hanging fruit? He said: It is and something like it with it, and there is a penalty, and there is no cutting in any of the hanging fruit, except for what He sheltered him in the two jinn, and whatever was taken from the two jinn and amounted to the price of the jinn, then it must be cut off, and if it did not reach the price of the jinn, it must be fined twice as much. \And stripes of cruelty.\"""""
"7153","7199 Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Salama bin Abdul Malik Al-Awsi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and he Ibn Salih, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “No cutting in the fruit, nor too much.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7154","7200 Amr bin Ali informed us, saying: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban. On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no cutting of fruit, nor of increasing it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7155","7201 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: He said: Rafi’ ibn Khadij: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “There should be no cutting of the fruit, nor any increase in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7156","7202 Muhammad bin Ma’dan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Yahya Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no cutting of fruit, nor of increasing it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7157","7203 Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban said: Rafi’ ibn Khadij said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No cutting off the fruit, or too much.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7158","7204 Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not cut the fruit, or multiply it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7159","7205 Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no cutting of fruit, nor of increasing it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7160","7206 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya. Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There should be no cutting in the fruit, nor in increasing it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7161","7207 Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, saying: Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi’ bin Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no cutting in the fruit.” \And not much.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7162","7208 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No cutting of fruit, nor multiplying, and plentiful: pebbles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7163","7209 Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Saeed bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Maymun, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No He cut off fruit, but not in abundance.” He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman: This is a mistake. It was narrated by Abu Usama, and he said on the authority of a man from his people (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7164","7210 Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of a man from his people, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No cutting of fruit, nor “a lot” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7165","7211 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, that a man from his people He narrated to him, on the authority of a paternal aunt of his, that Rafi’ ibn Khadij said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no cutting in the fruit, nor too much.”"
"7166","7212 Abdullah bin Abdul-Samad bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Mukhlid, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no punishment for a traitor or an embezzler.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan did not hear it from Abu al-Zubayr."
"7167","7213 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A traitor, a plunderer, or an embezzler does not have any right to do so.”"
"7168","7214 Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: I am Suwayd, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, on the authority of Jabir, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He turned away from the plunderer, the embezzler, and the outright traitor.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: What He did something that Ibn Jurayj did not hear from Abu al-Zubayr with us, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7169","7215 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr said, Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The one who plunders does not have to cut off anything.”"
"7170","7216 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said, Abu Al-Zubayr said, Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The embezzler does not have to be cut off.”"
"7171","7217 Ibrahim told me. He said: Hajjaj told us. He said: Ibn Jurayj said. Abu al-Zubayr said. Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The traitor does not have to be cut off.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith was narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Issa ibn Yunus, and al-Fadl ibn Musa, Ibn Wahb, Muhammad Ibn Rabi’ah, Mukhlid Ibn Yazid, and Salamah Ibn Sa’id. None of them said about him: Abu told me Al-Zubayr, and I do not think he heard it from Abu Al-Zubayr, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7172","7218 Al-Hussein bin Issa told me, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Warqa bin Omar Al-Khurasani, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim Al-Khurasani told us On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “There is no cutting off from an embezzler.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim is not strong regarding Abu Al-Zubayr, and he has nothing but an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7173","7219 Khalid bin Ruh told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Khalid bin Yazid bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, he said: he told us Shababah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Not for an embezzler. Nor a plunderer, nor an absolute traitor.”"
"7174","7220 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “There is no traitor.” Cut.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ash’ath ibn Siwar is weak and his hadith cannot be used as evidence. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7175","7221 Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Hammad told us, Yusuf said: on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hatib, “The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A thief was brought and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of God, he only stole. Then he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of God. He only stole. He said: Cut off his hand. He said: Then he stole, and his leg was cut off. Then he stole during the reign of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, until it was cut off. He stole all of his lists, then he also stole the fifth, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knew about this. When he said: Kill him, then he gave him to young men from Quraysh so that they would kill him. Among them was Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, and he loved women, so he said: Command me. \So they appointed him over them"
"7176","7222 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Aqeel told us, he said: My grandfather told us, he said: Mus’ab bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: “A thief was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Kill him, so they said: O Messenger of God, he only stole. He said: Cut him, so he was cut, then he was brought a second time and said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of God, he only stole. He said: They cut him, so he was cut, and he was brought a third time, and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of God, he only stole, so he said: Cut him, and he was brought. The fourth, he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of God, he only stole. He said: Cut him, so he was brought the fifth, and he said: Kill him. He said: Jabir, so we took him to the breeding place, and we carried him, and he lay on his back, then he broke his hand and leg, and the camels cracked, then they carried The second time, he did the same, then they attacked him the third time and threw stones at him, killing him. Then we threw him into a well, then we threw stones upon him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Mus’ab ibn Thabit is not strong, and Yahya al-Qattan did not abandon him, and this hadith is not Authentic, and I do not know of an authentic hadith on this subject from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7177","7223 Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told me, he said: Nafi’ bin Yazid told me, he said: Haywa bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, he said: I heard Busr bin Abi Artat, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Hands should not be cut off while travelling.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is not something to be used as evidence."
"7178","7224 Al-Hasan bin Mudarrak told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is Ibn Hammad, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Omar, and he is Ibn Abu Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If a slave is stolen, sell him, even if it is for a pound.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7179","7226 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ali, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, he said: I asked Fadalah bin Ubaid, “about hanging the hand of a thief around his neck.” He said: It is a Sunnah for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to cut off the hand of a thief. And he hung his hand around his neck.”"
"7180","7227 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Bin Muhayriz, he said: I said to Fadalah bin Ubaid: “Have you seen that hanging the hand around the neck of the thief, is it part of the Sunnah?” He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought. He greeted a thief, cut off his hand and hung it around his neck. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7181","7228 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Hassan bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid said: I heard Saad bin Ibrahim narrating, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The person who commits theft will not be fined if the punishment is imposed on him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is mursal and not proven."
"7182","7229 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, and Al-Harith bin Maskin Reading to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik. He said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi told me Sa`sa`ah, he said: I heard Sa`id bin Yasar Abu al-Hubab, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who God will return to him the good that befalls him.” The wording is by Al-Harith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7183","7230 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Saad bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik. On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The likeness of a believer is like raw material from the crop. The wind once blows it up and straightens it.” “Another, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like a cedar tree, nothing can strengthen it until it reaps a harvest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7184","7231 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah and Nuh bin Habib informed us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar informed us On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The likeness of a believer is like a crop. The wind will continue to warm it, the believer will continue to be afflicted by calamity, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like a cedar tree, which is shaken until it is harvested.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7185","7232 Qutaibah bin Saeed and Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, and the pronunciation is his, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: I said: “Which people are most severely tested?” He said: The prophets, then the best, then the best. The servant will be tested according to his religion. If his religion was solid, his trial would become severe, and if there was tenderness in his religion, he would be tested according to his religion. The trial would not cease to befall the servant until he left it. He walks on the earth who has no sin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7186","7233 Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abtar told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayfah, On the authority of his paternal aunt, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afflicted with a severe fever, so he ordered watering, so he was hung from a tree, then he lay down under it. So he started dripping on his heart and said: The most afflicted people are the prophets, then the best, and the next. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7187","7234 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was very ill. I said: O Messenger of God, you are You become very ill, is that because you have two rewards? He said: Yes, in the same way no Muslim is afflicted with harm from illness or anything else except that he disbelieves. God will remove his evil deeds from him, just as a tree sheds its leaves.”"
"7188","7235 Ibrahim bin Muhammad informed us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I have never seen pain more severe for anyone than it was for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7189","7236 Wahb bin Bayan informed us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no calamity that befalls a believer, except that he disbelieves, even if he is pricked by a thorn.”"
"7190","7237 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “No thorn or anything befalls a believer, but God recompenses him for his sin.”"
"7191","7238 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Bishr bin Umar, he said: Malik told us, And the word for it is, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whatever befalls “The believer has anything from a prick, even a thorn, unless God repays it for it, or expiates some of his sins because of it.”"
"7192","7239 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, he said: Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Aisha said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or anything above it, but God raises him one degree because of it, and takes away a sin from him because of it.”"
"7193","7240 Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya al-Qattan, on the authority of Sa’d, who is Ibn Ishaq, he said: Zainab told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, “ A man said: O Messenger of God, what do we have to do with these diseases? He said: Expiations. My father said: And if you say so? He said: Even a thorn."
"7194","7241 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Imran Abu Bakr told us, he said: Ata bin Abi Rabah told me, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: “Shall I not show you a woman from the people of Paradise?” I said: Yes, he said: This black woman, she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so she said to him: I have epilepsy, and I feel sick, so call upon God. He said: If you wish, you may be patient and Paradise is yours, and if you wish, I may pray to God. May he recover you. She said: Be patient. She said: I am uncovered, so pray to God that I do not uncover. So he prayed for her."
"7195","7242 Al-Hussein bin Muhammad informed us, saying: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a Bedouin: Did Umm Muldam take you? He said: O Messenger of God, and what is Umm Muldam? He said: O Messenger of God, I did not find this. He said: O Bedouins, has this headache bothered you? Messenger of God, and what is a headache? He said: Veins that strike a person in his head. He said: I did not experience this. When he left, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. And peace be upon him: Whoever likes to look at a man from the people of Hell, let him look at this one. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7196","7243 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, saying: Waki’ told us, And Bishr bin Al-Sirri, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Relieve the afflicted, feed the hungry, and minister to the sick.”"
"7197","7244 Suleiman bin Mansour informed us, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do seven things, and forbade us to do seven things. He ordered us to visit the sick person, and to follow Funerals, praising the one who sneezes, fulfilling oaths, extending greetings, supporting the oppressed, responding to the supplicant, and forbidding us: from the Khawatim Gold, and silver vessels, and copper, and brocade, and silk.”"
"7198","7245 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: I am Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: Abu Musa came to Al-Hussein bin Ali, to visit him and he was complaining, so Ali said: Did you come normally or complaining? He said: No, rather it is normal. He said: For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever is hostile to his brother will walk in the illusion of Paradise until He sits, and when he sits, mercy overwhelms him. If it is in the morning, seventy thousand angels pray over him until the evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray over him. A thousand angels until morning.”"
"7199","7246 Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin. A reading was read to him while I was hearing, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill, so I entered upon them and said: O Abu Bakr, how do you find yourself, and O Bilal, how do you find you? She said: It was Abu Bakr, when a fever seized him, would say: Every person goes to his family, and death is closer than the strap of his sandal, and Bilal was like this when he took it off. He raises his head and says to her: I wish I could spend the night in a valley, and around me is Idhkhar and Jalil, and did I ever want the waters of a spring? They look to me like a mole and an infant. Aisha said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, and he said: Oh God, make me dear to us. Medina is as we loved Mecca, or more strongly, and it is authentic. Harithah said in a hadith: Ours, and bless for us its fasts and its tides, and remove its fever. And make it with a hilt.”"
"7200","7247 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Husayn told me, he said: I heard Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayfah narrates, on the authority of his aunt Fatima, that she said: “We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some women to visit him, and lo, behold, a He was covered with severe fever. I said: O Messenger of God, if you pray to God and He reveals you, he says: Indeed, he is one of the most afflicted people: The prophets, then those after them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7201","7248 Utbah bin Abdullah informed us, saying: I read to Malik bin Anas and Al-Harith bin Miskin a reading to him while I was listening. On the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Atik, that Atik bin Al-Harith told him, Jabir ibn Atik informed him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came to ‘Awud Abdullah ibn Thabit, and found him defeated, so he shouted about him.” He did not answer him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned and said: We have defeated you, O Abu Al-Rabi’. So the women sat down and wept, so he made Ibn Atik kept them quiet, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Leave them, and when it becomes necessary, do not cry as much. They said: And what Obligation, O Messenger of God. He said: Death. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7202","7249 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: “I fell ill. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr visited me while they were walking, and they came to me while I had fainted, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution. Peace be upon him: Then he poured some of his ablution on me, and I said: O Messenger of God, how should I spend my money? He did not answer me with anything until the verse of inheritance was revealed: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “God gives you a fatwa.” Ibn al-Munkadir said: Jabir said: About me this was revealed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7203","7250 Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, saying: Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon a Bedouin who was visiting him, and said: “There is no problem with you if you purify yourself, God willing.” He said: “Yes.” It is a fever bubbling up in the bones of an old man, as if graves visit him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Well then.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7204","7251 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: A partner told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “A Jewish boy was serving the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he fell ill, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited him and said: Say: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God, so the boy looked at his father and said: Say what Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, says to you, and he said, and when he died, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Pray for your brother,” or he said: “Pray for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7205","7252 Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me, not riding a mule or a parasite.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7206","7253 Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid told him that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “one day rode a donkey with velvet covers on it, and Usama bin Zaid was riding it back.” Saad bin Ubadah was with Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and that was at the Battle of Badr. He passed by a council in which Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul was present, before His conversion to Islam, and in the gathering there was a mixture of Muslims and polytheists, so when the gathering was covered by the beast of the beast, Ibn Ubayy covered his nose with his robe. Then he said: Do not be arrogant against us. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted them, then he called them and read to them the Qur’an, and Ibn Ubayy said to him: There is nothing better than what you say, so do not return us to our gatherings, and return to your journey. Whoever comes to you, tell the story to him. Ibn Rawaha said: Yes, O Messenger of God, let us cheat in our assemblies, for we love that. The Muslims and the polytheists turned away, until they were about to fight, so he reduced them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until they remained silent, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked until he entered upon Saad bin Ubadah and said: What is Saad? Did you not hear what Abu Al-Hubab said? So he told him what happened, and Saad said: O Messenger of God, pardon him, and forgive him, by what has been revealed to you. The Book: God has brought to you the truth which He has revealed to you, and the people of this lake have agreed to crown him and surround him with a bandage. So God responded to that with the truth that He revealed to you.”"
"7207","7254 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was feeling sick, so I touched him and said: O Messenger of God, you are very sick. severely, so he said: I am feeling weak as two men among you are weak, and in the hadith I said: “Indeed, you will have two rewards.” He said: Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul everything that is on the earth. “If a Muslim is afflicted with harm, such as illness or anything else, God will remove his sins from him, just as a tree sheds its leaves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7208","7255 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’id, he said: Aisha bint Saad told me, Saad said: “I complained badly in Mecca, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to visit me, and he put his hand on my forehead and wiped my face.”"
"7209","7256 Bishr bin Khalid informed us, he said: I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was feeling ill. I said: O Messenger of God, you are very ill. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I am weak, and you are weak with two men. I said: Do you have two rewards? He said: Yes, or yes, then he said: None? “If a Muslim is harmed by a thorn or above, God will remove his sins from him, just as a tree sheds its leaves.”"
"7210","7257 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, saying: I am Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He returned a Muslim man who had become like a chick, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Were you not calling for anything or asking him? He said: Yes, I used to say: O God, whatever You punish me for in the Hereafter, grant it to me in this world, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Didn’t you say: Oh God, our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. He said: So he prayed to God, and God healed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7211","7258 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, he said: I am Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, on the authority of her father, “He complained in Mecca, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to visit him, and he said: Call on God, O Messenger of God, to reveal my name. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for him and said: O God, reveal Sa’d, by which you will benefit people, and by which you will harm. \people\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7212","7259 Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sick person came, he would pray for him: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal You are the Healer. There is no cure except Your healing. A cure that does not leave behind a disease.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7213","7260 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Abu Numan told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Aisha, she said: “When a sick person or a sick person was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would say: Remove the affliction, my Lord. People, and heal, you are the healer, there is no cure except your healing, a healing that does not leave behind an illness.”"
"7214","7261 Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Muslim. Ibn Subaih, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited a sick person, he would say: Go with courage.” Lord of the people, and heal You are the Healer, there is no cure except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness behind.”"
"7215","7262 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muawiyah bin Hisham, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Umayyah bin Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, said: Sahl bin Hanif and I went out to look for wine. We found wine and a tavern, and one of us was ashamed for anyone to see him. He said: So he hid himself from me until when he saw that he had done so, he removed a grain of wool and entered. water, so I looked at him and I liked his appearance, so I hit him with an eye, and a rumbling took him over. I called him but he did not answer me, so I came to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So I told him the news, and he said: Arise with us. So he came to him and lifted himself from his leg, and it was as if I were looking at clear white He drove him while he was running towards him until he came to him and said: Oh God, remove her heat and pour water on her. Then he said to him: Get up, so he got up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you sees something about himself, his property, or his brother that he likes, let him pray for blessings."
"7216","7263 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited him while he was not of sound mind, so he performed ablution and some of his ablution was poured on him, and he became of sound mind, so I said: He will inherit my calamity. So what about the inheritance? Then the verse of obligation was revealed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7217","7264 Masoud bin Juwayriyah informed us, saying: Al-Mu’affa told us, meaning Ibn Imran, on the authority of Hisham, the companion of Al-Dastawa’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: “I complained that I have seven sisters, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and sprinkled water on my face, so I woke up and said: O Messenger By God, I bequeath two-thirds to my sisters. He said: Better. I said: Half. He said: Better. Then he went out and left me, then came back and said: O Jabir. I do not see you dying from this pain of yours. Indeed, God has sent down, and He has made it clear to your sisters, and has given them two-thirds. Jabir said: So this was revealed. Verse: Say, “May God give you a fatwa concerning the calamity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7218","7265 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, “Some people entered upon the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They returned to him, and the time for prayer came and he prayed with them sitting, so they stood up and he motioned to them to sit down. When he finished his prayer, He said: The imam was appointed to be followed, so when he prays standing, they pray standing, and when he kneels, they kneel, and if he prays sitting, they pray sitting."
"7219","7266 Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Taffawi told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “ The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was knocked down from his horse and his colt colts, so they entered upon him to visit him, so he prayed with them while sitting, and they stood up and he gestured. He told them to sit, and when he had finished his prayer, he said: The imam is only to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar,” “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bows, “so bow.” He prostrated, so prostrate, and when he prayed standing, they pray standing, and when he prayed, they pray sitting, all together.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7220","7267 Zakaria bin Yahya informed me, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and there were men in the house, including Omar bin The speech, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come, I will write for you a letter after which you will never go astray. Then Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. He was overcome with pain, and with you is the Qur’an. The Book of God is sufficient for us. So they gathered in the house, and some people said: Arise, and it will be written for you. A book after which you will never go astray. And some people said what Omar said, and when the confusion and disagreement increased before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said To them: “Stand up from me.” Ubayd Allah said: Ibn Abbas used to say: The tribulation is all the tribulation that has passed from the book that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended. May God bless him and grant him peace. It is decreed that you will never go astray after him, when their confusion and disagreement increased."
"7221","7268 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must wish, let him say: O God, grant me life as long as life is good.” For me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.”"
"7222","7269 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’id bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid He says: “My aunt took me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, my sister’s son was in pain and he wiped my head. He prayed for my blessing, then he performed ablution and I drank from his ablution, then I got up behind his back and looked at his ring between his shoulders like a button. \hopscotch\"""""
"7223","7270 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, his companions complained, and he complained Abu Bakr, Amer bin Fuhayra, Abu Bakr’s client, and Bilal. So Aisha asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to visit them. So he gave her permission, and she said to Abu Bakr: How do you find yourself? He said: Every person goes to his family and death is closer than the trap of his sandal. I asked Amer. Ibn Fuhayra, and he said: I saw death before I tasted it. The coward died from above. I asked Bilal, and he said: I wish my hair had been made better. One night in a valley, and around me are Idhkhar and Jalil. And will I ever see spring waters? And do they appear to me as a mole and a tufayl? So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I told him what they said, and he looked at the sky and said: O God, make Medina beloved to us, O God, bless for us its Sa’a. And stretch it out, and move its fever to a sanctuary, which is Al-Juhfa.”"
"7224","7271 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us, that Anas bin Malik told us He told them that people or men from Ukal and Uraynah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and spoke Islam, and they said: O Messenger of God. By God, we are the people of Dara’, and we do not have a countryside. They took advantage of the city, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered for them land and pasture land. He ordered them to go out there and drink from its milk and urine. When they woke up and were near Al-Harra, they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and sought shelter. The news reached the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he sent to search for them and they were brought. So they gouged out their eyes and cut off their hands and feet, then left them in the free country as they were until they died.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7225","7272 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi’ah, that Omar went out to the Levant until, when they were near Sarg, he heard that The epidemic occurred in the Levant, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you heard of it, On land, do not approach it, and if it falls on land while you are there, do not escape from it.” Then Omar returned from Sarg."
"7226","7273 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin. It was read to him while I was hearing, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that Abdul Rahman bin Awf said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If you hear of it on a land, do not approach it, and if it occurs on a land while you are on it, do not escape from it.” \""
7227"""
"7227","Mahmud ibn Ghaylan informed us, saying: Waki' narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Malik, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""This plague is a punishment (rijz) and a remnant of a punishment with which a people were afflicted. So if it breaks out in a land while you are in it, do not flee from it; and if it breaks out in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it."""
"7228","7275 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Amir bin Sa’d, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned the plague, and said: “A remnant of affliction and torment sent upon a group of the Children of Israel, so when it strikes a land while you are there Do not leave it, and if it falls on land and you are not there, do not land on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7229","7276 Al-Harith bin Miskin. A reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: I am Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, and Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he heard him ask Usama bin Zaid, what did you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the plague? Usama bin Zaid said, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The plague is a scourge sent upon a group of the Children of Israel and upon whomever they are.” Before you, if you hear about it, do not enter, and if it occurs on land while you are there, do not leave to escape from it.” Malik said: He said: Abu Al-Nadr: Fleeing from it will not get you out of it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7230","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a recitation of it while I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, He said: I am Malik, on the authority of Na’im al-Mujmar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “At the gates of Medina are angels. Neither the plague nor the antichrist will enter it.”"
"7231","7278 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, and Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Abu Yunus told us, he said: Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, That she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the plague? Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed her: “It was a punishment that God sends upon whomsoever He wills, and He has made it a mercy for the believers. A servant falls into the plague, and he stays in his country, patient and seeking hope, knowing that nothing will befall him except what God has decreed for him, unless he will have a similar reward. \martyr\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7232","7279 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “There are five martyrs: the one who was stabbed, the one who drowned, the one who destroyed it, and the martyr in the path of God.”"
"7233","7280 Utbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I read to Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin read to him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Atik, that Atik bin Al-Harith told him that Jabir Ibn Abdullah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Martyrdom is seven things, apart from killing in the path of God: the stabbed is a martyr.” The one who is lined is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one who destroys is a martyr, the one who has a sideburn is a martyr, and the one who burns is a martyr. And the woman dies with a martyr’s plural, meaning postpartum childbirth.”"
"7234","7281 Ziyad bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. He used to recite to himself the exorcists and blow his nose. When his complaint became severe, I began to recite and breathe over him, and wipe over him with my hands, hoping for her blessing.”"
"7235","7282 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Shuraih bin al-Nu’man told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: She Aisha: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill, so I placed his hand on his chest and said: Go away, Lord of people, you are the doctor. And you are the healer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Join me with the highest companion, and join me with the highest companion.”"
"7236","7283 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ya’la told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: “We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thirty men with a group at night, but they refused to host us, so I came down to a camp. Then their master was stung, so they came to us and said: Is there anyone among you who performs ruqyah? We said: Yes. They said: So go. We said: No, unless you prepare for us a ruqyah. You refused to host us, so they gave us thirty sheep, so I went with them and began to recite the Fatihah of the Book, and wiped the place that had been bitten. Until he recovered, so they gave us the sheep, and I said: By God, we will not eat. I do not know what ruqyah is, nor am I the best of ruqyah. So when we came, we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So we informed him, and he said: How do you know that it is a ruqyah? And you did not know that it was a ruqyah. Yes, so eat it and collect for me. With you by an arrow.” Hushaym disputed it, and narrated it on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id"
"7237","7284 Ziyad bin Ayyub informed us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: I am Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, “Indeed, people from The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were on a journey, and they passed through an Arab neighborhood. They hosted them, but they refused to host them. So someone among them was bitten or bitten, so they said to the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there anyone among you who is a tyrant? Then a man among them said: Yes, I am. So their companion was brought to me with the opening of the book, and he was healed. He was given a flock of sheep, but he refused to accept it, until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So that was mentioned to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I did not recite it except with the opening of the book. He laughed, He said: How do you know that it is a ruqyah? Then he said: Take the sheep and hit me with an arrow with you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7238","7285 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Kharijah bin Al-Salt, on the authority of his uncle, said: We came from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we came to an Arab neighborhood, and they said: Do you have any medicine or ruqyah? Indeed, with us is an idiot who is in chains, so they brought an idiot in chains, so I recited to him the opening of the Book for three days, morning and evening, I gather Then I spit out my sputum, as if it had been squirted from a headband. So they gave me a lump, and I said: No, so they said: Ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I asked him. He said: Eat, for by my life, whoever eats a telegram of falsehood has eaten a telegram of truth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7239","7286 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Bishr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Umair, the client of Abul Lahm, he said: “I witnessed Khaybar with My masters, they spoke about me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that I am a slave, so he ordered me to draw the sword, and I will reward him. So he ordered me to bring some of his belongings. He said: I showed him a ruqyah with which I used to recite ruqyah for the insane, so he ordered me to cast some of it, and he was detained. \some of it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7240","7287 Amr bin Mansour told me, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Shaddad On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to seek protection from the spring.”"
"7241","7288 Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Urwa bin Amer, on the authority of Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, that Asma bint Umays said: I said: “O Messenger of God, the Banu Ja’far are afflicted by the evil eye. Should I seek protection?” To them? He said: Yes, and if anything preceded fate, the evil eye would precede it."
"7242","7289 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Mas’ar said, we told him, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, He said: “My mother made broth, and it spilled on my hands. So my mother took me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said something that I did not remember, so I asked her. On the authority of Uthman: What did he say? She said: He said: Remove the evil, Lord of the people, and heal, and you are the healer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7243","7290 Muhammad ibn Rafi’ informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Abd informed us. Al-Rahman, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger granted May God bless him and grant him peace in the ruqyah from every person with a fever.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7244","7291 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “A man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of God Is there a ruqyah for a scorpion? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7245","7292 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yahya bin Adam informed me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Yusuf, who is the son of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for ruqyah against the evil eye and fever. And the ant"
"7246","7293 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Sulayman bin Abi Hathmah, on the authority of Hafsa, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon her and there was with her a woman called Al-Shifa, a derivation of an ant, and he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Teach her Hafsa. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7247","7294 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: I am Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told us. Ibn Abdul Aziz, he said: Saleh Ibn Kaysan told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr Ibn Sulaiman Ibn Abi Hathamah, that Al-Shifa’ was the daughter of Abdullah, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while I was sitting at Hafsa’s house. He said: Don’t you teach this ruqyah for an ant? Did you teach her to write? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7248","7295 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I Malik and the wording for him, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained He recited the supplications to himself and blew his nose. When his pain became severe, I used to recite the supplications to himself and wipe over him.” In the hadith of Al-Harith: On his authority with his hand. Hope for her blessing"
"7249","7296 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: She said: Aisha: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained about his family, he would wipe him with his right hand and say: Remove the violence, Lord of the people. Heal, you are the healer, there is no cure except your healing, your healing does not leave behind a disease.”"
"7250","7297 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Kaab, that Nafi’ bin Jubayr told him on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me to relieve me of pain. He became strong with me and said: Wipe your right hand seven times, and say: I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from the evil I find. I did so, and God will remove it. “It was with me, and I continued to order it to my family and others.”"
"7251","7298 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, then he mentioned a word that means, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, On the authority of Abu Saeed, “Some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a neighborhood of the Arabs, but they did not approach them, so while they were like that, When the master of those people was stung, he said: Is there a medicine or a potion among you? Then he said: You will not bring us peace, so we will not do so until you make us a reward. So they made for themselves a herd of goats, and he began to recite the Mother of the Qur’an, collect its slugs, and spit. The man recovered, so they brought the goats, and they said: We will not take it until we ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. He laughed and said: What? Do you know that it is a ruqyah? Take it and shoot me with an arrow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7252","7299 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to blow his nose during ruqyah.”"
"7253","7300 Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained, he would recite to himself the exorcists and blow his nose."
"7254","7301 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Rabbo, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to say to the sick person like this, sprinkling his spit on the ground with his finger, and saying: “In the name of God, the soil of our land, spit it out.” Some of us, our sick will be healed, with the permission of our Lord.”"
"7255","7302 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to perform ruqyah, saying: “Eliminate the evil, Lord of the people, there is no one to remove it except You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7256","7303 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeks refuge, saying: Wipe away the calamity, Lord of the people. There is no cure except your cure, a cure that leaves no sickness behind."
"7257","7304 Ismail bin Masoud and Muhammad bin Abd al-A’la informed us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, that Ziyad bin Ulaqah narrated to them. He said: I heard Usama bin Sharik saying: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, his companions were with him as if there were birds on their heads. The Bedouins came and asked him, and they said: Did you seek treatment? He said: Get treatment, for God did not create a disease without creating a cure for it, other than one thing. Ismail in his hadith: Al-Haram (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7258","7305 Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf, told me, he said: Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Usama bin A partner, he said: “I witnessed the Bedouins asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about things in which there is no harm: Is there anything wrong with us in such-and-such? Messenger of God? Is there a burden on us in such and such? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O servants of God, may God remove the burden, except for a man who committed a crime. Muslim, that is a hardship. They said: Have you sought treatment, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes, for God has never placed a disease on the earth without sending down a cure for it, other than a disease. One. They said: O Messenger of God, what is it? He said: Al-Haram?"
"7259","7306 Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr and Muhammad bin Lamthanna informed us, on the authority of Abu Ahmad, who said: Umar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not sent down any disease but He has sent down a cure for it.” The wording is victory. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7260","7307 Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I am Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every disease has a cure, so if the cure for the disease is applied, he will be cured, God willing.”"
